# 0013: the panel upload switch, and W1.5 -- the layer uploads the host alone needs
#
# The fifth stage asked one question first: is the picture of a --no-panel boot the host's own replay,
# or is it the composed display surface (0xFFFF0001) the guest uploads every frame?  A boot-arg,
# glwire_nopanel_up=1, stops that upload and changes nothing else; the boot that answered it is in
# docs/gpu-acceleration-stage5-results.md section 1 (a desktop, 38.1% not black, with no panel
# upload in the whole run).
#
# The rest is W1.5, the other half of "the host draws the frame": remote_only stops running the
# recorded calls here, which also stopped the layer textures from ever reaching the host (the fourth
# stage's R3: 0 image refs, a black screen).  upload_changed_layers() sends the non-target IOSurfaces
# by reference instead -- no Mesa texstore here -- and my_glBindTexture() no longer refills a target
# image from the guest's stale surface, which would paint over what the host just drew into it.
#
# What it did not fix, measured: the labels under the icons, the dock and the search field are not in
# the record at all (CoreAnimation's software path draws them), so a remote_only screen is 245 KB
# instead of 448 KB.  That boundary is the next stage's first decision.
#
# Apply from the root of the working tree:
#   patch -p1 < patches/0013-stage5-nopanel-and-w15.patch
--- a/userland/src/eagl.c
+++ b/userland/src/eagl.c
