--- /dev/null
+++ b/userland/rc.touch1
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# rc.touch1 -- one touch process, and nothing else of this round's: the fifth stage's S4.
+#
+# rc.drive (six rwtouch processes, the first of them at 120/150/480 s) panicked four cold boots out
+# of four in the fourth stage while the same kernel without a touch process passed five of five. So
+# the variables come out one at a time: this file has ONE rwtouch process, whose first action is at
+# 600 s (a boot's first frame is five to nine minutes after the kernel starts), and the same driven
+# gesture S5 needs -- the Settings icon, then twenty seconds of its list -- so that a boot that
+# passes also gives the measurement window.  rc.touch2 is this one with `noqos` (the interactive
+# thread class taken out).
+#
+#   /tmp/<label>.log        rwtouch: mark scroll-start / scroll-end are the window's edges
+#   tools/glwire/harness/fps.py reads them, and the driver's own "MiniIOMobileFramebuffer: N frames
+#   in M ms" lines inside.
+
+/redwood/bin/vtop_test &
+
+/redwood/bin/netcfg en0 10.0.2.15 10.0.2.2 &
+
+/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 600 mark touch-start tap 0.656 0.729 wait 90 mark scroll-start zigzag 0.5 0.74 0.26 2000 10 mark scroll-end &
+
+# and then hand process 1 to the real launchd, as rc.launchd does
+exec /sbin/launchd.darwin
